Tell Wine where the embedded editor window is as soon as it is mapped

yabridge only tells Wine the embedded window's screen position when the host
window sends a ConfigureNotify, and only with the size from a ConfigureNotify
on the parent window. A host that creates the editor window at its final size
and position (JUCE with a plugin whose editor reports its size immediately,
e.g. IK Multimedia Hammond B-3X) never generates either, so Wine keeps the
window at (0,0) and every click reaches the plugin offset by the window's
screen position; the translated event also carried a 0x0 size, which Wine
ignores. Push the real position and size on MapRequest and when the host
window changes, and fall back to xcb_get_geometry for the parent's size.

Verified with WINEDEBUG=+msg: WM_LBUTTONDOWN lParam equals the window-relative
click before and after moving the window, for Hammond B-3X and Kontakt 8.
---
diff --git a/src/wine-host/editor.cpp b/src/wine-host/editor.cpp
index 835cd18..18cae33 100644
--- a/src/wine-host/editor.cpp
+++ b/src/wine-host/editor.cpp
@@ -479,6 +479,41 @@ std::array<int16_t, 2> Editor::get_parent_window_offset() {
     return {coord_reply->dst_x, coord_reply->dst_y};
 }
 
+void Editor::send_wine_window_position() {
+    const std::array<int16_t, 2> offset = get_parent_window_offset();
+
+    xcb_generic_error_t* error = nullptr;
+    const xcb_get_geometry_cookie_t geometry_cookie =
+        xcb_get_geometry(x11_connection_.get(), parent_window_);
+    const std::unique_ptr<xcb_get_geometry_reply_t> geometry(
+        xcb_get_geometry_reply(x11_connection_.get(), geometry_cookie, &error));
+    THROW_X11_ERROR(error);
+    if (!geometry || geometry->width == 0 || geometry->height == 0) {
+        return;
+    }
+
+    xcb_configure_notify_event_t translated_event{};
+    translated_event.response_type = XCB_CONFIGURE_NOTIFY;
+    translated_event.event = wine_window_;
+    translated_event.window = wine_window_;
+    translated_event.width = geometry->width;
+    translated_event.height = geometry->height;
+    translated_event.x = offset[0];
+    translated_event.y = offset[1];
+    logger_.log_editor_trace([&]() {
+        return "DEBUG: Pushing Wine window position: " +
+               std::to_string(translated_event.width) + "x" +
+               std::to_string(translated_event.height) + "+" +
+               std::to_string(translated_event.x) + "+" +
+               std::to_string(translated_event.y);
+    });
+    xcb_send_event(x11_connection_.get(), false, wine_window_,
+                   XCB_EVENT_MASK_STRUCTURE_NOTIFY |
+                       XCB_EVENT_MASK_SUBSTRUCTURE_NOTIFY,
+                   reinterpret_cast<char*>(&translated_event));
+    xcb_flush(x11_connection_.get());
+}
